Insertion at Kth Position — Book Revision

To insert a node at the kth position, create a new node with value X. If K == 1, connect the new node to the current head using newNode.next = head and return newNode because it becomes the new head. Returning newNode does not return only its value; since newNode.next points to the old head, the complete remaining list is connected and can be traversed. Otherwise, move current to the node just before position K, connect newNode.next = current.next, then connect current.next = newNode, and return the original head.

Time: O(k) — traverse up to position K; worst case O(n).
Auxiliary Space: O(1) — only pointer variables and the new node are used.

code
=================================

class Solution {
    public ListNode insertAtKthPosition(ListNode head, int X, int K) {

        // Create the new node
        ListNode newNode = new ListNode(X);

        // If inserting at the 1st position,
        // new node becomes the head
        if(K == 1){
            newNode.next = head;
            return newNode;
        }

        // Start from the head
        ListNode current = head;

        // Move current to the node just before position K
        for(int i = 1; i < K - 1; i++){
            current = current.next;
        }

        // Connect new node to the next node
        newNode.next = current.next;

        // Connect current node to new node
        current.next = newNode;

        // Return the original head
        return head;
    }
}
